class.description:
A selection is a list of primitive indices, not a copy of the geometry. Filtering and splitting build new selections without touching any geometry; only [method get_surface] assembles anything, and only for the primitives the selection holds.

Selections chain, which is how one mesh output becomes one node per instance name with one surface per material:
[codeblock]
var by_material = surfaces.filter_by("hego_visible", 1).split_by("hego_material")
for material in by_material:
    var surface = by_material[material].get_surface(["hego_lod", "hego_col_type"])
[/codeblock]

Obtained from [method HEGoGeoSurfaces.select_all], [method HEGoGeoSurfaces.filter_by] or [method HEGoGeoSurfaces.split_by].
